From 01b93aa39850605dde31ad31f8462307ee4731f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas <yusenrong46@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:25:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Show reported chat activities in the Home and Journey
 garden

Inline activity reports were written only to activity_sessions, while Home and
Journey read legacy reflections/outcomes, so a person's chat check-ins never
appeared there. A read-only, owner-scoped GET /v1/activity-history returns a
minimal projection of reported sessions (no note, link, instructions or model
text). The gardens merge it with legacy check-ins; plants grow only from the
person's own rating, 'not tried' stays a seed, and a history failure leaves legacy
check-ins visible.

Tests: tests/test_activity_history_api.py (owner isolation, privacy, order, bounds),
journey unit cases, and the PostgreSQL integration test now checks the history
through PostgREST/RLS and on the Journey page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
